[?25l> The build compiles successfully. Here's a summary of what was created:

Cargo.toml — depends on openssl crate (for AES-256-ECB used by the NIST DRBG)

src/main.rs — single-file translation containing:
- All SPHINCS+ SHA2-128f-simple parameters and constants
- SHA-256 incremental hashing (from sha2.c)
- MGF1-SHA256 and seed_state (from sha2.c)
- Address manipulation functions (from address.c)
- Utility functions: ull_to_bytes, u32_to_bytes, bytes_to_ull, compute_root (from utils.c)
- Hash functions: initialize_hash_function, prf_addr, gen_message_random, hash_message (from hash_sha2.c)
- thash simple variant (from thash_sha2_simple.c)
- AES-256-CTR-DRBG RNG: randombytes_init, randombytes (from rng.c)
- WOTS: gen_chain, base_w, chain_lengths, wots_pk_from_sig, wots_gen_leafx1 (from wots.c, wotsx1.c)
- FORS: fors_sign, fors_pk_from_sig, fors_gen_leafx1 (from fors.c)
- Treehash: wots_treehashx1, fors_treehashx1 (from utilsx1.c)
- Merkle: merkle_sign, merkle_gen_root (from merkle.c)
- Sign/verify: crypto_sign_keypair, crypto_sign, crypto_sign_open (from sign.c)
- KAT transcript (SHA2 variant) and main() (from PQCgenKAT_sign.c)

The code uses unsafe only for the global DRBG state (matching C's global DRBG_ctx). The address byte manipulation uses pointer casts to match C's (unsigned char *)addr pattern. To build, set OPENSSL_LIB_DIR and OPENSSL_INCLUDE_DIR if pkg-config doesn't find OpenSSL automatically.✓ Created checkpoint 1



